  "Question": "\\(\\left(4^{-1}-3^{-1}\\right)^{-1}=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-12\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac1{12}\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "For any nonzero number \\(x\\), \\(x^{-1}=1/x\\). First calculate the expression inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n4^{-1}-3^{-1}\n=\\frac14-\\frac13\n=\\frac3{12}-\\frac4{12}\n=-\\frac1{12}.\n\\]\nThis value is nonzero, so the outer exponent \\(-1\\) takes its reciprocal:\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac1{12}\\right)^{-1}=-12.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(-12\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
